API Catalog

Centralized Repository: Maintains a comprehensive list of all APIs within the organization.

Discovery & Reuse: Enables teams to easily discover existing APIs for reuse, reducing duplication.

Metadata & Classification: Provides key details such as versioning, ownership, dependencies, and classifications (e.g., internal, partner, public).

Governance & Compliance: Supports governance by enforcing standards, naming conventions, and lifecycle management.

Visibility: Enhances transparency and accountability across API development teams.

API Marketplace

Internal & External Exposure: Offers a platform to expose APIs to internal teams, partners, or third parties.

Self-Service Access: Allows consumers to browse, evaluate, and subscribe to APIs with minimal friction.

Monetization (Optional): Supports API usage tracking and monetization strategies for partner or public APIs.

Developer Engagement: Enhances developer experience with easy onboarding, usage guides, SDKs, and analytics.

Security & Access Control: Integrates with authentication and authorization mechanisms to manage secure access.
